TIP:  In the intro/outro and instrumental bridge you play (Am7) like an (Am) with your pinky added to the bottom string/3rd fret.  In the chorus you play it with two fingers or, you can not play it at all.

TIP:  The (C6) is just (Am) with your pinky added to the 5th string/3rd fret.  So in the intro you play start with (D) and quickly move to (Am), then add your pinky, then remove it to get back to (Am), etc.

TIP:  The chords in |brackets| mean strike once (or two or three times as indicated) which emulate the horns prior to the chord.

TIP:  In the chorus, for that first |C| - |Cmaj7| - |C| just lift off the index finger from the (C).  And in the second line, from the (Am) to the (Am7) lift off the ring finger.

TIP:  When played live, Neil ends with “Sweet Car – o – line” with the |D/A| played on the first syllable.  It’s just (D) with your pinky added to the 4th string/4th fret.


